            "lastname": "Devenport",
            "title": "Chief Executive Officer",
            "bio": "Ed Devenport is the CEO and co-owner of Incipio Group which was founded in 2015. Incipio Group is a UK hospitality group which specialises in transforming forgotten and overlooked spaces into beautiful venues that defy convention. The independent group operates some of London’s most popular F&B destinations including Pergola, The Prince and Lost in Brixton and is recognised at being at leading seasonal activations within the sector, attracting over 2.5 million guests per year. \n\nNow operating 7 venues in London with 3 more to open in 2022, Ed leads a team that specialise in building, converting and renovating all manner of venues from temporary pop-up spaces to permanent destination venues, always with the aim of redefining the way people, eat, drink and socialise. Incipio frequently change their drinking and dining concepts and regularly transform their venues to ensure every guest feels ‘somewhere else’, whether it’s their first visit or their tenth. All done under the Incipio mantra of providing great times in beautifully curated vibrant atmospheres.\n\nIn September 2022 Incipio Group will open their eighth venue, a 450 capacity bar and restaurant located in the vaults of The Royal Exchange which was built in 1566. \n",
