            "title": "Special Board Advisor, eathos",
            "bio": "Andy Holman has 40+ years of International restaurant expertise across 30+ countries having held increasingly senior leadership roles in Operations, Marketing, Business Development, C Suite & Board advisory. \n\nFollowing 5 years as CEO, and now acting as a specialist advisor to the board of eathos, a highly specialised restaurant group, incorporating International franchise brands SushiArt, Tortilla, Kababji, Rosa Thai, Cocotte and The Athenian, as well as locally developed brand Joga and crafted ‘Virtual’ brands Mashrou3 Tabkha, Alien Burger, The Burger Fix and Up Brands.\n\nIn addition to running traditional Brick & Mortar restaurants, eathos has developed numerous next generation Virtual brands, which it operates through 3rd party & own facility cloud kitchens.  \nBefore returning to Dubai in 2018 to join eathos, Andy oversaw the development of food concepts into new markets, as a part of Minor International, with specific responsibility for establishing ‘Fine Dining’ & ‘Casual Dining’ Thai concepts in the UK & Europe.\n\nThis followed seven years as the Managing Director for Thailand & Vice President of International Franchising for The Pizza Company, Thailand’s largest pizza & pasta restaurant chain, where he oversaw the growth from 100 to over 450 Restaurant & Delivery outlets.\n\nBetween 1995 & 2006, whilst based in Dubai, Andy was responsible for leading the growth of Pizza Hut in the MENAPAKT region from around 100 stores to over 600. \n\nPrior to this, he spent 15 years working in a diverse selection of restaurants, bars, clubs & hospitality venues across the UK, initially as a means to survive after being expelled from school but rapidly because he fell in love with the industry…(and a girl who still tolerates him after 38 years!) \n\nDespite a relatively early exit from formal academia, Andy completed a Management Development Program at Cornell University but has learned the majority of what he considers to be really valuable by working alongside colleagues & customers in the Hospitality industry......mostly that he loves food in all forms and (most of) the people involved in producing it, moving it, serving it & consuming it.\t",
