            "bio": "An  experienced  architect, urban  planning  expert and  an  inspiring young Emirati  leader  focused  on promoting a culture of entrepreneurship, innovation and facilitating strategic foreign investments. Abdullah Al Abdooli is the Chief Executive Officer of Marjan, the master-developer of freehold properties in Ras Al Khaimah. \n\nAs CEO of Marjan, Abdullah drives the strategic growth initiatives of the company, with a focus on developing   world-class   master-planned   communities   in   Ras   Al   Khaimah   that   will   attract   foreign investment  and  position  the  emirate  as  a  regional  investment  and  tourism  hub. \n\nHe  is  responsible  for identifying new opportunities for growth, expanding Marjan’s partnerships to global  markets  and helping   create   a   strong   framework   that   enhances   investor   confidence. He   also   manages   the development,   operations and   expansion   plans   for   Al   Marjan   Island   to   ensure   that   the project contributes to the economic development of the Emirate. Abdulla is credited with several innovative initiatives that have enhanced the reputation of Ras Al Khaimah globally including the New Year’s Eve Fireworks that welcomed hundreds of thousands of visitors to the emirate and has clinched Guinness World Records.\n\nDrawing on his competencies in real estate development and urban master-planning, he was Director of Town Planning and Survey Administration and Director of Project Management Office at RAK Municipality. Previously, he  was also  a  Board  Member  of the  RAK  International  Airport  Authority  and RAK Sewerage Authority.\nAbdulla holds a Masters in Regional & Urban Planning from the Paris Sorbonne University in Abu Dhabi and graduated  from  the  American  University  of  Sharjah. He  also earned  a certificate in Real  Estate Investment Strategies from Harvard University.",
