            "bio": "In my role as Vice President Global Guest Technology and Innovation, I provide technical and functional expertise on the tools used in hotels and define a strategic plan with the Hubs to prioritize product evolution in guest facing technology and drive innovation across all brands and regions.\n\nI also drive product adoption in the Hubs and provide technical and functional expertise on guest technology.\n\nMoreover, I am responsible to animate a community and define the technology standards guidelines to be used and adapted by different Accor brands globally.\n\nI joined Accor as Regional Director Customer Technology Services IMEA in 2019. I have a wealth of experience and expertise in technology for Operations, holding senior positions in Rotana Hotels & Resorts and Mövenpick Hotels & Resorts. \n\nIn my most recent role, I and my Area Directors team were in-charge of the day-to-day management and support of hotel IT operations, ensuring that hotels meet Accor IT brand standards and benefit from the technological innovation that is transforming the hospitality industry.\n\nI hold a master’s degree in computer science and am pursuing my Executive MBA with City University of London. I am also ITIL and CDCP certified.\n\n\n",
